-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, section 102(b), (c), (d) and (f) (piece dg1): what the
-- certificate of incorporation may also contain, which powers need not be set out, provisions that depend on
-- facts outside the certificate, and the ban on stockholder liability for the fees of an internal corporate
-- claim. Layer 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Section 102(a) is in dg1-s102a-required-contents.l4 and subsection (e) in dg1-s102e-name-reservation.l4.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.

§ `Section 102(b) -- What the certificate of incorporation may also contain`

-- In addition to the matters subsection (a) requires, the certificate "may also contain any or all of" the matters
-- paragraphs (b)(1) to (7) list: none of them is required.
-- src:48 | (b) In addition to the matters required to be set forth in the certificate of incorporation by subsection (a) of this section, the certificate of incorporation may also contain any or all of the following matters:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b) (src:48)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b) the certificate of incorporation is required to contain the matter listed in subsection (b)` MEANS FALSE

