-- No stockholder has a preemptive right unless, and except to the extent that, it is expressly granted in the
-- certificate. Rights in existence on July 3, 1967 remain unaffected by the paragraph unless and until changed or
-- terminated by appropriate action which expressly provides for the change or termination. A right "in existence
-- on" that date is one that arose on or before it.
-- src:54 | No stockholder shall have any preemptive right to subscribe to an additional issue of stock or to any security convertible into such stock unless, and except to the extent that, such right is expressly granted to such stockholder in the certificate of incorporation. …
-- src:54 | All such rights in existence on July 3, 1967, shall remain in existence unaffected by this paragraph unless and until changed or terminated by appropriate action which expressly provides for the change or …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(3) (src:54)
GIVEN `the right is expressly granted to the stockholder in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the right came into existence` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the right has been changed or terminated by appropriate action which expressly provides for the change or termination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(3) the stockholder has a preemptive right to subscribe to an additional issue of stock or to a convertible security` `the right is expressly granted to the stockholder in the certificate of incorporation` `the date on which the right came into existence` `the right has been changed or terminated by appropriate action which expressly provides for the change or termination` MEANS
        `the right is expressly granted to the stockholder in the certificate of incorporation`
     OR (CONSIDER `the date on which the right came into existence`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST arose THEN
                 (arose AT MOST `s 102(b)(3) the date on which existing preemptive rights are preserved`)
             AND (NOT (`the right has been changed or terminated by appropriate action which expressly provides for the change or termination`)))

§§ `s 102(b)(4) A larger vote than this chapter requires`

-- "The vote of a larger portion of the stock or of any class or series thereof, or of any other securities having
-- voting power". A requirement is larger if it is counted against the same base and has a larger proportion, or the
-- same proportion that must be exceeded where the chapter's is reached. Against different bases the text does not
-- compare them (NOTHING).
-- src:55 | (4) Provisions requiring for any corporate action, the vote of a larger portion of the stock or of any class or series thereof, or of any other securities having voting power, or a larger number of the directors, than is required by this chapter;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(4) (src:55)
GIVEN `the vote this chapter requires` IS A `Vote requirement`
      `the vote the certificate of incorporation requires` IS A `Vote requirement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(4) the certificate of incorporation requires a larger portion of the stock or other securities having voting power than this chapter requires` `the vote this chapter requires` `the vote the certificate of incorporation requires` MEANS
    IF `the vote this chapter requires`'s `counted against` EQUALS `the vote the certificate of incorporation requires`'s `counted against`
    THEN JUST (    (`the vote the certificate of incorporation requires`'s proportion GREATER THAN `the vote this chapter requires`'s proportion)
               OR (    (`the vote the certificate of incorporation requires`'s proportion EQUALS `the vote this chapter requires`'s proportion)
                   AND `the vote the certificate of incorporation requires`'s `must be exceeded`
                   AND (NOT (`the vote this chapter requires`'s `must be exceeded`))))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:55 | (4) Provisions requiring for any corporate action, the vote of a larger portion of the stock or of any class or series thereof, or of any other securities having voting power, or a larger number of the directors, than is required by this chapter;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(4) (src:55)
GIVEN `the number of the directors this chapter requires` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the directors the certificate of incorporation requires` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(4) the certificate of incorporation requires a larger number of the directors than this chapter requires` `the number of the directors this chapter requires` `the number of the directors the certificate of incorporation requires` MEANS
    `the number of the directors the certificate of incorporation requires` GREATER THAN `the number of the directors this chapter requires`

§§ `s 102(b)(5) The duration of the corporation's existence`

-- A limit on the duration to a specified date; otherwise the corporation has perpetual existence. The corporation's
-- duration has expired on a day after the specified date (the specified date itself is inside the duration).
-- src:56 | (5) A provision limiting the duration of the corporation’s existence to a specified date; otherwise, the corporation shall have perpetual existence;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(5) (src:56)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(5) the duration of the corporation's existence has expired` `the day in question` `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST limit THEN `the day in question` GREATER THAN limit

-- src:56 | (5) A provision limiting the duration of the corporation’s existence to a specified date; otherwise, the corporation shall have perpetual existence;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(5) (src:56)
GIVEN `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(5) the corporation has perpetual existence` `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the certificate of incorporation limits the corporation's existence`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST limit THEN FALSE

§§ `s 102(b)(6) Personal liability of stockholders for the debts of the corporation`

-- A provision may impose personal liability for the debts on the stockholders to a specified extent and upon
-- specified conditions (the extent is whatever the provision specifies: it is not computed here). Otherwise the
-- stockholders are not personally liable for the corporation's debts, except as they may be liable by reason of
-- their own conduct or acts.
-- src:57 | (6) A provision imposing personal liability for the debts of the corporation on its stockholders to a specified extent and upon specified conditions; otherwise, the stockholders of a corporation shall not be personally liable for the payment of the corporation’s debts except as they may be liable by reason of their own conduct or acts;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(6) (src:57)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision imposing personal liability for the debts of the corporation on its stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions upon which the provision imposes liability are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder is liable by reason of the stockholder's own conduct or acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(6) the stockholder is personally liable for the payment of the corporation's debts` `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision imposing personal liability for the debts of the corporation on its stockholders` `the conditions upon which the provision imposes liability are met` `the stockholder is liable by reason of the stockholder's own conduct or acts` MEANS
        (    `the certificate of incorporation contains a provision imposing personal liability for the debts of the corporation on its stockholders`
         AND `the conditions upon which the provision imposes liability are met`)
     OR `the stockholder is liable by reason of the stockholder's own conduct or acts`

