    `the date of the act or omission`                                                                              IS A DATE
    `the date when the provision becomes effective`                                                                IS A DATE

-- A provision may eliminate or limit the personal liability of a director or officer to the corporation or its
-- stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty as a director or officer, but it shall not
-- eliminate or limit the liability of: (i) a director or officer for a breach of the duty of loyalty; (ii) a
-- director or officer for acts or omissions not in good faith or involving intentional misconduct or a knowing
-- violation of law; (iii) a director under section 174 (piece dg3); (iv) a director or officer for a transaction
-- from which the person derived an improper personal benefit; (v) an officer in any action by or in the right of the
-- corporation. Nor shall it eliminate or limit liability for an act or omission before the date when it becomes
-- effective. "Director" includes a person who exercises the board's powers under the certificate (section 141(a),
-- piece dg2); "officer" means only a person deemed to have consented to service under 10 Del. C. § 3114(b) (Title
-- 10, an input). An "officer" who has not so consented is not within the paragraph, and neither is a liability that
-- is not to the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty (NOTHING).
-- src:58 | (7) A provision eliminating or limiting the personal liability of a director or officer to the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty as a director or officer, provided that such provision shall not eliminate or limit the liability of:
-- src:59 | (i) A director or officer for any breach of the director’s or officer’s duty of loyalty to the corporation or its stockholders;
-- src:60 | (ii) A director or officer for acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law;
-- src:61 | (iii) A director under § 174 of this title;
-- src:62 | (iv) A director or officer for any transaction from which the director or officer derived an improper personal benefit; or
-- src:63 | (v) An officer in any action by or in the right of the corporation.
-- src:64 | No such provision shall eliminate or limit the liability of a director or officer for any act or omission occurring prior to the date when such provision becomes effective.
-- src:66 | All references in this paragraph (b)(7) to a director shall also be deemed to refer to such other person or persons, if any, who, pursuant to a provision of the certificate of incorporation in accordance with § 141(a) of this title, exercise or perform any of the powers or duties otherwise conferred or imposed upon the board of directors by this title.
-- src:67 | All references in this paragraph (b)(7) to an officer shall mean only a person who at the time of an act or omission as to which liability is asserted is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to § 3114(b) of Title 10 (for purposes of this sentence only, treating residents of this State as if they were nonresidents to apply § 3114(b) of Title 10 to this sentence).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(7) (src:58-64) (src:66-67)
GIVEN l IS A `s 102(b)(7) Liability asserted`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(7) the provision may eliminate or limit the person's personal liability` l MEANS
    -- out of range: section 174 (piece dg3), section 141(a) (piece dg2) and 10 Del. C. § 3114(b) (Title 10)
    IF    (l's capacity EQUALS `as an officer`)
       AND (NOT (l's `the officer was at the time of the act or omission deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to § 3114(b) of Title 10`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (l's `the liability is to the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty as a director or officer`)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF l's `the date of the act or omission` LESS THAN l's `the date when the provision becomes effective`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST (NOT (   l's `the liability is for a breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or its stockholders`
                              OR l's `the liability is for acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law`
                              OR (    (NOT (l's capacity EQUALS `as an officer`))
                                  AND l's `the liability is under § 174 of this title`)
                              OR l's `the person derived an improper personal benefit from the transaction`
                              OR (    (l's capacity EQUALS `as an officer`)
                                  AND l's `the liability is asserted in an action by or in the right of the corporation`)))

-- An amendment, repeal or elimination of such a provision does not affect its application to an act or omission
-- occurring before the amendment, repeal or elimination, unless the provision provides otherwise at the time of
-- the act or omission. For an act on or after the amendment the provision as amended is what applies.
-- src:65 | An amendment, repeal or elimination of such a provision shall not affect its application with respect to an act or omission by a director or officer occurring before such amendment, repeal or elimination unless the provision provides otherwise at the time of such act or omission.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(b)(7) (src:65)
GIVEN `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination of the provision` IS A DATE
      `the provision provides otherwise at the time of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(b)(7) the provision as it stood continues to apply to the act or omission despite the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `the date of the act or omission` `the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination of the provision` `the provision provides otherwise at the time of the act or omission` MEANS
        (`the date of the act or omission` LESS THAN `the date of the amendment, repeal or elimination of the provision`)
    AND (NOT (`the provision provides otherwise at the time of the act or omission`))

