§ `Section 102(d) -- Provisions dependent on facts ascertainable outside the certificate`

-- src:69 | (d) Except for provisions included pursuant to paragraphs (a)(1), (a)(2), (a)(5), (a)(6), (b)(2), (b)(5), (b)(7) of this section, and provisions included pursuant to paragraph (a)(4) of this section specifying the classes, number of shares, and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue, any provision of the certificate of incorporation may be made …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(d) (src:69)
DECLARE `s 102(d) Provision of the certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the name of the corporation under paragraph (a)(1)`
    `the registered office and registered agent under paragraph (a)(2)`
    `the incorporators under paragraph (a)(5)`
    `the first directors under paragraph (a)(6)`
    `the compromise or arrangement provision under paragraph (b)(2)`
    `the limit on the duration of the corporation's existence under paragraph (b)(5)`
    `the elimination or limitation of the liability of a director or officer under paragraph (b)(7)`
    `the classes, number of shares and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue under paragraph (a)(4)`
    `any other provision of the certificate of incorporation`

-- Except for the provisions the paragraph lists, any provision of the certificate may be made dependent on facts
-- ascertainable outside the instrument, provided that the manner in which the facts operate upon the provision is
-- clearly and explicitly set forth in it. The list reaches the (a)(4) provision on classes, shares and par value only
-- for a corporation other than a nonstock corporation.
-- src:69 | (d) Except for provisions included pursuant to paragraphs (a)(1), (a)(2), (a)(5), (a)(6), (b)(2), (b)(5), (b)(7) of this section, and provisions included pursuant to paragraph (a)(4) of this section specifying the classes, number of shares, and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue, any provision of the certificate of incorporation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside such instrument, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the provision is clearly and explicitly set forth therein. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(d) (src:69)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 102(d) Provision of the certificate`
      kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the manner in which the facts operate upon the provision is clearly and explicitly set forth in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(d) the provision may be made dependent on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` provision kind `the manner in which the facts operate upon the provision is clearly and explicitly set forth in the certificate` MEANS
        `the manner in which the facts operate upon the provision is clearly and explicitly set forth in the certificate`
    AND (CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `the name of the corporation under paragraph (a)(1)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the registered office and registered agent under paragraph (a)(2)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the incorporators under paragraph (a)(5)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the first directors under paragraph (a)(6)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the compromise or arrangement provision under paragraph (b)(2)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the limit on the duration of the corporation's existence under paragraph (b)(5)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the elimination or limitation of the liability of a director or officer under paragraph (b)(7)` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the classes, number of shares and par value of shares a corporation other than a nonstock corporation is authorized to issue under paragraph (a)(4)` THEN `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
         WHEN `any other provision of the certificate of incorporation` THEN TRUE)

-- "The term 'facts,' as used in this subsection, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event,
-- including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation." The list is not
-- exhaustive, so a matter of another kind is not decided (NOTHING).
-- src:69 | The term “facts,” as used in this subsection, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(d) (src:69)
DECLARE `s 102(d) Matter outside the certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of an event`
    `a determination by a person or body, including the corporation`
    `an action by a person or body, including the corporation`
    `a matter of another kind`

-- src:69 | The term “facts,” as used in this subsection, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(d) (src:69)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 102(d) Matter outside the certificate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102(d) the matter is a fact on which a provision may depend` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `the occurrence of an event` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination by a person or body, including the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an action by a person or body, including the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a matter of another kind` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 102(f) -- No liability of a stockholder for the fees or expenses of the corporation or another party`

-- The certificate may not contain a provision that would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees
-- or expenses of the corporation or any other party in connection with an internal corporate claim, as defined in
-- section 115 (dg1-s111-s115-jurisdiction-and-forum.l4), or in connection with any other claim that a stockholder,
-- acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or
-- proceeding.
-- src:76 | (f) The certificate of incorporation may not contain any provision that would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys’ fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party in connection with an internal corporate claim, as defined in § 115 of this title, or in connection with any other claim that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 102(f) (src:76)
GIVEN `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 102(f) the certificate of incorporation may contain the provision` `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party` `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding` MEANS
    NOT (    `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party`
         AND (   `s 115(b) the claim is an internal corporate claim` `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim`
              OR `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding`))
